\section*{Shub entropy conjecture}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
A noninvertible $C^1$ self-map of a closed smooth manifold is claimed to have zero topological entropy although its second-homology action has eigenvalue two, disproving the general $C^1$ entropy inequality. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Mathematical claim 1.} For some integer $q>0$, OpenAI claims a continuously differentiable self-map $f$ of
\[
M=(\mathbb R/100\mathbb Z)\times(S^2)^{q+1}
\]
with zero topological entropy and an eigenvalue $2$ on $f_*:H_2(M;\mathbb R)\to H_2(M;\mathbb R)$. Thus
\[
h_{\mathrm{top}}(f)=0<\log2\le\log\rho(f_*).
\]
The map need not be invertible. The spectral radius is for the induced real-homology action; the claim is a $C^1$ self-map counterexample rather than a smooth diffeomorphism counterexample.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 151, 2026-09-25): A slowing circle clock controls a main sphere map and a collection of signal registers. A uniformly differentiable infinite prediction series forces every orbit toward two zero-entropy invariant sets; a direct separated-set argument localizes entropy there, while projection retains degree two on homology without providing a dynamical factor map.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 151, 2026-09-25): The selected C1 self-map conjecture does not require invertibility. The paper’s compact-manifold example has entropy zero and a real homology eigenvalue two, directly contradicting its logarithmic spectral-radius lower bound.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 151, the scope page documents the following selections. The selection gives a noninvertible map with $C^1$ regularity, zero topological entropy, and an eigenvalue-two vector in second real homology. It does not supply a smooth or invertible counterexample. The documented statement covers the main claim of manuscript 1. Its selected declaration also covers the clause used for this problem. Comparator files: C1EntropyCounterexample.lean. Declarations: OAI.Problem340.exists\_C1\_entropy\_counterexample.

This site has not executed the Lean files or checked their dependencies. These descriptions report the scope of the linked declarations, rather than a new verification of the proofs.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these results to an internal model. Its release notice cautions that results lacking full formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently assessed the proofs; a solved label records the scope of the reported claim.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item OpenAI, \emph{A C\({}^{1}\) Counterexample to the Entropy Conjecture}, 2026-09-25; citation key \texttt{OAI:A-C1-Counterexample-to-the-Entropy-Conjecture-September-25-2026}. \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-C1-Counterexample-to-the-Entropy-Conjecture-September-25-2026/article.pdf}{PDF (GitHub)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/raw/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-C1-Counterexample-to-the-Entropy-Conjecture-September-25-2026/article.pdf}{PDF (direct)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-C1-Counterexample-to-the-Entropy-Conjecture-September-25-2026/README.md}{Manuscript page and citation}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/A-C1-Counterexample-to-the-Entropy-Conjecture-September-25-2026/article.pdf}{Latest version}; Statement source: \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-C1-Counterexample-to-the-Entropy-Conjecture-September-25-2026/build/source/main.tex\#L98}{thm:main}.
\item Family 151: \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/docs/151.md}{Lean scope}.
\item \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/ComparatorChallenges/C1EntropyCounterexample.json}{Comparator C1EntropyCounterexample.json}.
\item \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/ComparatorChallenges/C1EntropyCounterexample.lean}{Comparator C1EntropyCounterexample.lean}.
\item \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/CONTENTS.md}{OpenAI catalogue entry}.
\end{itemize}
